		{
			"id": "110301124993634782",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://front-end.social/@Fyrd/110301124955219308",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alexis Deveria",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@Fyrd",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/363/502/817/699/134/original/0d08d4f26d5ff9ba.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-05-02T21:06:39.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> No plans right now, though I know MDN BCD is thinking about it.</p><p>From experience there'll be a number of poor souls to whom the information will still be valuable for some time to come so that's why I'm not in a hurry to do so, might switch to hiding by default first.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110301136256417623",
			"parentId": "110301124993634782",
			"url": "https://front-end.social/@ppk/110301136192886929",
			"author": {
				"name": "ppk 🇪🇺",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@ppk",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/293/034/668/175/414/original/c0d4895d91ab41e8.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-05-02T21:09:30.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@Fyrd\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>Fyrd</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Four years ago someone thanked me for the IE5.5 coverage on my site. She worked on some godawful SAP system where IE5.5 was still the default browser. In 2019. And no one else had any info about it.</p><p>There are niche markets for which access to ancient browser info is important. And it doesn't hurt anyone to keep the info in place.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
