		{
			"id": "110301155916850835",
			"parentId": "110301136256417623",
			"url": "https://front-end.social/@Fyrd/110301155814678520",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alexis Deveria",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@Fyrd",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/363/502/817/699/134/original/0d08d4f26d5ff9ba.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-05-02T21:14:29.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@ppk\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>ppk</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Wow. But yeah, that's basically my thoughts too. I do get that people would appreciate a stance that no devs should have to worry about supporting IE anymore, but it'd also be nice to keep around for the rare edge case here and there.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110301167485284205",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@tomw/110301167415434005",
			"author": {
				"name": "Tom Walker",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@tomw",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/338/280/995/838/214/original/fbcf1ae1c2f82118.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-05-02T21:17:26.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> In principle I'm in favour of not supporting IE, in practice I did it for a site a couple of years ago and quickly received \"site doesn't work\" support emails from... you guessed it.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "110301181279962447",
			"parentId": "110301121743844793",
			"url": "https://front-end.social/@Fyrd/110301181250660851",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alexis Deveria",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@Fyrd",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/363/502/817/699/134/original/0d08d4f26d5ff9ba.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-05-02T21:20:58.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://metalhead.club/@flori\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>flori</span></a></span> Yeah if you go to <a href=\"https://caniuse.com/ciu/settings#display\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">caniuse.com/ciu/settings#displ</span><span class=\"invisible\">ay</span></a> and select \"Filtered\" all tables will default to 0.5%+ usage which will also hide IE.</p><p>Further customization possible by adding a new browser set under <a href=\"https://caniuse.com/ciu/settings#browsers\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">caniuse.com/ciu/settings#brows</span><span class=\"invisible\">ers</span></a></p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
